            "review_title": "Review at Upper Saigon",
            "review_text": "Simeon T\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam182 contributions\n0\nAverage Bar\nApr 2017 • Friends\nLocated within a hotel on one of the top floors, it has a fairly good vantage point of the city skyline. The challenge was that they had a bar blocking the vantage point. The rest of the seating area was OK but, comfortable.\n\nThe music selection was very average and the DJ was slamming songs together that didn't make sense and weren't in sync with one another.\n\nService was below average as it took quite a long time to flag a waiter down to order a drink. The drinks took even longer to get there and weren't that great. They were watered down with way too much ice. When it came settling the bill it took just as long to find someone who would actually give us the bill and get us change.\n\nI would understand if the place was jam packed with people but, it wasn't busy for a Friday night.\n\nAll in all, I wouldn't recommend going to this place when there are plenty of better bars and lounges in the city.\nRead more\nWritten July 27, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
